# Vite `import.meta.env.*` values, read at BUILD time. Nothing here is a
# secret (Worker-side secrets live in `.dev.vars`). Copy this file to `.env`
# for local dev — `.env` is gitignored so a real key can't leak and a stale
# test key can't be shipped to production by accident.
#
# Deployed environments do NOT read this file: each Workers Builds project
# sets `VITE_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY` as its own build variable (production => the
# real site key from its Turnstile widget; staging => the test key below).
# A build with the var unset ships a widget that can't render — a loud
# failure, on purpose.
#
# Cloudflare's test keys (https://developers.cloudflare.com/turnstile/troubleshooting/testing/):
#   always-pass:  site 1x00000000000000000000AA / secret 1x0000000000000000000000000000000AA
#   always-fail:  site 2x00000000000000000000AB / secret 2x0000000000000000000000000000000AA
VITE_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=1x00000000000000000000AA
